{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":498169,"name":"Rob","username":"ras434","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/ras434/{size}/120070_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-22T13:00:34.028Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Grok Bot 0.57.1 for macOS, local-exec continues to flap: the daemon stays up, but ListMachines can return empty and its log shows repeated user-computer-provider ConnectError / ECONNRESET / DeadlineExceededError stream/poll failures.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse Grok Bot with local-exec on macOS. During a turn, observe ListMachines and ~/.grokbot/local-exec-daemon.log. The daemon can remain alive for days while agent-visible machines intermittently disappear and the log accumulates the stream/poll failures.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe local-exec daemon should keep a stable provider stream/poll connection, and ListMachines should consistently show the registered Mac.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"attachment\" href=\"/uploads/short-url/dRmsQAbz9fgsNC5gpWfvHkKft5H.txt\"\u003elocal-exec-daemon-redacted.txt\u003c/a\u003e (4.47 KB)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-operating-system-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-operating-system-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-version-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-version-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot 0.57.1\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot local-exec\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot available anymore (from the interrupted turn).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-additional-information-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-additional-information-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/dean\"\u003e@Dean\u003c/a\u003e Rie — follow-up on \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-computers-local-exec-still-flapping-after-update/170488\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eGrok Bot Computers / local-exec still flapping after update\u003c/a\u003e as a separate thread per your ask.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChecked today (Tue 2026-09-22, America/New_York):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eResidual is still happening. After the Sep 6 ~1:51pm ET mid-work self-heal on 0.43.0, I also saw at least one agent-visible ListMachines empty around Sep 10 ~11:39am ET. App is now \u003cstrong\u003e0.57.1\u003c/strong\u003e. Daemon process can stay up for days, but \u003ccode\u003e~/.grokbot/local-exec-daemon.log\u003c/code\u003e still fills with \u003ccode\u003euser-computer-provider\u003c/code\u003e \u003ccode\u003eConnectError\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003eECONNRESET\u003c/code\u003e / \u003ccode\u003eDeadlineExceededError\u003c/code\u003e stream/poll failures (no “desktop ownership lost” storm in the current long-lived process — flapping form shifted).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLog caveat: \u003ccode\u003elocal-exec-daemon.log\u003c/code\u003e has \u003cstrong\u003eno timestamps\u003c/strong\u003e, so I cannot isolate “2 minutes before the ~1:51pm ET drop through recovery.” Attached is a redacted recent contiguous excerpt of the same pattern under 0.57.1.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRequest ID from that interrupted turn: I don’t have it anymore. Happy to add if I can recover it.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdate Track: not visible in local settings files (no Early Access / releaseChannel keys). UI is Stable vs Nightly on my build — I can confirm which I’m on if needed.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHardware (PII-light): MacBook Pro M2 Pro 32GB, macOS 26.x — same as the prior thread.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAttached: local-exec-daemon-redacted.txt\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-498169-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-11\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-498169-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-11\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-22T13:00:43.450Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":11,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":55.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":172658,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-local-exec-still-flapping-on-0-57-1-residual-from-170488","display_username":"Rob","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-computers-local-exec-still-flapping-after-update/170488","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Grok Bot Computers / local-exec still flapping after update","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136488,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-local-exec-still-flapping-on-0-57-1-residual-from-170488/172658/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":498286,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-22T15:12:03.385Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/ras434\"\u003e@ras434\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the follow-up thread and the log excerpt.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat you pasted matches a pattern we already have on our side. The helper on your Mac that keeps the connection to our servers occasionally loses its long-lived stream (a server rollout or a short network blip can both cut it). While it retries with a growing wait between attempts, the Mac can drop out of the list of computers for a minute or two before it comes back on its own. That is what the self-heal you saw looks like from our side, and it is tracked as something to fix on our end, not a problem with your setup.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne reassuring note: looking at your Mac from our side, the helper has been up continuously since the 0.57.1 update on Sep 19 and we see almost none of these drops since then. So the excerpt is most likely from before that.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo catch the next one with a time we can line up, could you try this once?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Terminal on the Mac.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePaste this and press Return, then leave the window open:\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003etail -F ~/.grokbot/local-exec-daemon.log | while IFS= read -r line; do printf '%s %s\\n' \"$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S %Z')\" \"$line\"; done \u0026gt;\u0026gt; ~/Desktop/local-exec-daemon-timestamped.log\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eKeep using Grok Bot as usual. The next time an agent says the Mac is unreachable or the computer list comes back empty, note the time (ET is fine).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn that chat, use the \u003ccode\u003e...\u003c/code\u003e menu next to a message and click Copy Request ID.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eReply here with the time, the Request ID, the lines from ~/Desktop/local-exec-daemon-timestamped.log from about 2 minutes before the drop through the recovery\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks again.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-22T15:12:03.385Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172658,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-local-exec-still-flapping-on-0-57-1-residual-from-170488","display_username":"Colin","primary_group_nam